  "title": "On a plane knot space the knot fails by counting faces, and selection is a line-face perfect matching",
  "subject": "The structure of the knot's solutions on a knot space whose incidence graph is plane, and what a handle changes",
  "conclusion": "With Kasteleyn signs a solution makes each line skip the corner opposite its odd point and every face hold an odd number of skipped corners, so Euler's n + 2 faces for n lines force failure and, after a removal, the solutions are the perfect matchings of the other lines to the faces off the removed line. Genus g removes 2g faces and adds 2g homology parities.",
